01:28:17,154 --> 01:28:20,646
Three rounds and you're a vegetable, aren't you, pikey!

1264
01:29:11,108 --> 01:29:14,236
I'm in charge here. No fucking about, no eye-gouging.

1265
01:29:14,445 --> 01:29:16,606
Do your worst. Let's get it on!

1266
01:29:48,079 --> 01:29:51,139
What the fuck's going on? You gonna finish him or what?

1267
01:30:33,157 --> 01:30:35,125
Talk about saved by the bell.

1268
01:30:35,693 --> 01:30:39,220
Do you understand the consequences of knocking that man out?

1269
01:30:39,430 --> 01:30:41,728
Do not knock him out, Mickey.

1270
01:30:48,339 --> 01:30:50,068
All right, let's break it up.

1271
01:31:24,075 --> 01:31:25,542
What, is he fucking deaf?

1272
01:31:26,944 --> 01:31:28,741
What is he doing?

1273
01:31:44,495 --> 01:31:45,894
Come on and sit.

1274
01:31:48,632 --> 01:31:50,623
What the fuck are you doing, Mickey?

1275
01:31:50,835 --> 01:31:52,962
You're dancing like a fairy.

1276
01:31:53,237 --> 01:31:55,899
They'll hang us if they think it's rigged.

1277
01:31:56,640 --> 01:31:58,801
Get out there and hurt him.

1278
01:32:00,177 --> 01:32:05,114
But for fuck's sake, do not knock him out.

1279
01:33:25,396 --> 01:33:28,331
All he's got to do is stay down.

1280
01:33:32,870 --> 01:33:35,065
Now, we are fucked.

1281
01:33:43,347 --> 01:33:44,336
He can't stand up.

1282
01:33:44,548 --> 01:33:45,378
We're out of here.

1283
01:33:45,583 --> 01:33:50,748
Stupid pikey knows Brick Top's got keen-to-kill monkeys with shotguns...

1284
01:33:50,955 --> 01:33:53,185
...sitting outside his campsite.

1285
01:33:53,390 --> 01:34:01,298
Once the campsite's wiped out, I know it's gonna be the same for us.

1286
01:34:01,298 --> 01:34:03,129
Ever cross the road and look the wrong way?

1287
01:34:03,334 --> 01:34:04,801
Give me that fucking shooter!

1288
01:34:05,002 --> 01:34:07,562
And, hey, presto, there's a car nearly on you.

1289
01:34:07,771 --> 01:34:08,931
So, what do you do?

1290
01:34:09,506 --> 01:34:11,599
Something very silly.

1291
01:34:11,976 --> 01:34:14,877
You freeze. And your life doesn't flash before you...

1292
01:34:15,112 --> 01:34:17,672
...because you're too scared to think.

1293
01:34:17,881 --> 01:34:21,009
You just freeze and pull a stupid face.

1294
01:34:21,218 --> 01:34:23,482
But the pikey didn't. Why?

1295
01:34:23,721 --> 01:34:26,519
Because he had plans on running the car over.

1296
01:34:28,892 --> 01:34:31,053
It had previously occurred to me...

1297
01:34:31,328 --> 01:34:34,263
...that he'd taken the demise of his mother rather lightly.

1298
01:34:38,002 --> 01:34:40,800
For every action, there is a reaction.

1299
01:34:41,405 --> 01:34:42,929
And a pikey reaction...

1300
01:34:43,607 --> 01:34:44,972
...is quite a fucking thing.

1301
01:35:26,984 --> 01:35:29,043
Pete, talk to me.

1302
01:35:29,286 --> 01:35:32,881
If you want your friend to hear you, talk a lot louder than that.

1303
01:35:41,799 --> 01:35:45,428
- Give me that fucking shooter. - I'll give you your shooter, you cunt.

1304
01:35:53,410 --> 01:35:57,107
That is when I thought the pikey had money riding on himself.

1305
01:35:58,115 --> 01:36:01,607
That's why the bastard never goes down when he's supposed to.

1306
01:36:03,420 --> 01:36:05,149
We've been tucked up...

1307
01:36:06,790 --> 01:36:08,417
...while he's been cleaning up.

1308
01:36:10,527 --> 01:36:13,155
We're worse off now than when we started.

1309
01:36:18,669 --> 01:36:21,137
The next day we went to the campsite...

1310
01:36:21,338 --> 01:36:24,501
...but the gypsies had disappeared during the night.

1311
01:36:24,708 --> 01:36:26,699
Which was probably a good thing...

1312
01:36:26,977 --> 01:36:31,209
...considering they'd just buried 12 people somewhere in the area.

1313
01:36:31,415 --> 01:36:33,042
Where is he?

1314
01:36:33,250 --> 01:36:35,480
He ain't fucking here, that's for sure.

1315
01:36:36,220 --> 01:36:39,747
We can't ask a man to fight for us if we can't find him, can we?

1316
01:36:39,957 --> 01:36:43,290
You won't find a pikey that doesn't want to be found.

1317
01:36:45,195 --> 01:36:48,426
He could be in a campsite in Kampu-fucking-chea by now.

1318
01:36:50,033 --> 01:36:51,864
Bollocks! Come on.

1319
01:36:57,107 --> 01:36:59,905
- What you doing here? - What's it got to do with you?

1320
01:37:03,781 --> 01:37:05,942
So, what you doing here?

1321
01:37:13,557 --> 01:37:16,424
I'm taking the dog for a walk. What's the problem?

1322
01:37:18,395 --> 01:37:19,327
What's in the car?

1323
01:37:19,897 --> 01:37:21,489
Seats and a steering wheel.

1324
01:37:22,332 --> 01:37:24,163
What do you know about gypsies?

1325
01:37:25,936 --> 01:37:27,927
I know they're not to be trusted.

1326
01:37:29,973 --> 01:37:32,737
All right, get your dog. On your way.

1327
01:37:33,510 --> 01:37:35,068
Get the dog, Tommy.

1328
01:37:37,147 --> 01:37:38,444
The dog.

1329
01:37:39,750 --> 01:37:44,278
All right, boy. Come on. Come on, Daisy. No, Daisy!

1330
01:37:45,255 --> 01:37:46,950
He loves that dog.

1331
01:37:47,291 --> 01:37:49,054
Always playing silly games.

1332
01:37:49,259 --> 01:37:52,660
Stop messing about and get it in the car. Tommy!

1333
01:37:55,332 --> 01:37:59,291
Good boy. Good boy. Good boy, Daisy, good boy.

1334
01:38:10,080 --> 01:38:11,638
Could you tell me...

1335
01:38:11,849 --> 01:38:15,114
...why you got a dead man with an arm missing in your boot?

1336
01:38:15,752 --> 01:38:16,741
Hey, George...

1337
01:38:18,121 --> 01:38:20,316
...is that a tea cosy on his head?

1338
01:38:23,694 --> 01:38:26,185
Oh, you love a dog, don't you, Tommy?

1339
01:38:36,039 --> 01:38:38,633
Tommy persuaded me to keep the dog.

1340
01:38:38,842 --> 01:38:42,107
I eventually agreed, as long as he took it to a vet.

1341
01:38:42,312 --> 01:38:45,213
I couldn't stand that squeaking anymore.

1342
01:38:45,482 --> 01:38:48,883
The vet found half an undigested shoe, a squeaky toy...

1343
01:38:49,119 --> 01:38:52,452
...and an 84-carat diamond lodged in its stomach.

1344
01:38:52,656 --> 01:38:55,523
It's quite amazing what can happen in a week.

1345
01:38:55,893 --> 01:38:57,884
Still didn't shut it up, though.

1346
01:38:58,795 --> 01:39:00,456
So, what do you do?

1347
01:39:00,664 --> 01:39:03,758
You go see the man that knows about these sort of things.

1348
01:39:03,967 --> 01:39:05,662
So, what do you think?

1349
01:39:07,271 --> 01:39:09,569
Do you know anyone who'd be interested?

1350
01:39:14,378 --> 01:39:15,367
I might.

